---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../../../components/Hero.astro";
import Figure from "../../../components/Figure.astro";
import Icon from "../../../components/Icon.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../../consts";
import heroImg from "../../../assets/photos/tokyo-odaiba-liberte-rainbow-bridge.webp";

interface MapSpot {
  eyebrow: string;
  name: string;
  address: string;
}

function mapsHref(spot: MapSpot) {
  return `https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=${encodeURIComponent(`${spot.name}, ${spot.address}`)}`;
}

const rainbowBridge: MapSpot = {
  eyebrow: "Odaiba",
  name: "Rainbow Bridge",
  address: "Minato City, Tokyo 105-0000, Japan",
};

const shutokoMapsHref = "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shuto+Expressway+Tokyo";

const hakoneTurnpikeMapsHref =
  "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=35.207272061897214,139.09176042856018";
---

<Layout
  title="Where to drive in Tokyo"
  description="The best roads to drive in Tokyo in a rental car: the Rainbow Bridge, Odaiba, the Shutoko and a getaway to Hakone."
>
  <Hero
    image={heroImg}
    eyebrow="Great spot · Tokyo"
    title="Where to drive in Tokyo"
    subtitle="A few roads to enjoy behind the wheel of your JDM, day or night."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <a
      href={withBase("/en/tokyo/")}
      class="tap-target link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink-soft"
    >
      <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      Back to Tokyo
    </a>

    <p class="reveal mt-8 font-body text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Renting a car in Tokyo is great. Knowing where to drive it is even better. Between the buildings of Odaiba, the
      elevated ramps of the Shutoko and a getaway to the mountains of Hakone, here are the roads that stuck with me the
      most during my stay.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Rainbow Bridge & Odaiba</h2>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      The Rainbow Bridge links the Shibaura district to the artificial island of Odaiba, and the crossing alone is
      worth it. Once on the other side, you're a stone's throw from Odaiba Beach, with a superb view of the bridge,
      both during the day and once night falls and its lights come on. There are several parking lots on Odaiba, all
      of them paid.
    </p>

    <div class="reveal mt-6 rounded-lg border border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/40 p-5">
      <p class="eyebrow text-racing-500">{rainbowBridge.eyebrow}</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{rainbowBridge.name}</p>
      <p class="mt-1 flex items-start gap-1.5 font-body text-sm text-ink-soft">
        <Icon name="map-pin" class="mt-0.5 h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 text-mist-500" />
        {rainbowBridge.address}
      </p>
      <a
        href={mapsHref(rainbowBridge)}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="tap-target link-underline mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
      >
        Open in Google Maps
        <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      </a>
    </div>

    <Figure
      image={heroImg}
      alt="Replica of the Statue of Liberty in Odaiba, with the Rainbow Bridge and Tokyo skyscrapers in the background"
      caption="Odaiba's Statue of Liberty replica, with the Rainbow Bridge in the background."
      class="mt-8"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The Shutoko expressway</h2>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      The Shuto Expressway (or Shutoko) is the urban expressway network that crisscrosses Tokyo, partly elevated,
      partly running along the bay. It was from one of its lanes that I crossed the Rainbow Bridge at night in the Evo
      VIII rented from OnlyJDM, engine roaring and city lights in the background: an experience in itself. The network
      is huge and lets you link several neighborhoods without a single red light.
    </p>
    <a
      href={shutokoMapsHref}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="tap-target link-underline mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
    >
      See the network on Google Maps
      <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
    </a>
    <br />
    <a
      href={withBase("/en/tokyo/only-jdm/")}
      class="tap-target link-underline mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
    >
      Read the article about renting from OnlyJDM
      <Icon name="arrow-right" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-10 sm:pb-14 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Further from Tokyo</h2>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      If you have a whole day ahead of you, two roads outside the city are worth the detour. The Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line
      crosses the bay for almost 15 km, first through an undersea tunnel and then over a bridge, to reach Chiba
      Prefecture. This is the road that leads to Umihotaru PA, an artificial rest area built right in the middle of the
      bay and famous for its car meets.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Even further, about 1 hour from Tokyo, the Anest Iwata Turnpike in Hakone (formerly the Hakone Turnpike) is a toll
      mountain road, famous among Japanese enthusiasts for its bends and its views of Mount Fuji and Sagami Bay.
    </p>

    <div class="reveal mt-6 rounded-lg border border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/40 p-5">
      <p class="eyebrow text-racing-500">Hakone</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Anest Iwata Turnpike</p>
      <a
        href={hakoneTurnpikeMapsHref}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="tap-target link-underline mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
      >
        Open in Google Maps
        <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="reveal mt-8 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      More roads will be added to this list over my next trips to Japan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/50 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 text-center sm:px-8">
      <a
        href={withBase("/en/tokyo/")}
        class="tap-target link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        Back to all Tokyo spots
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
